Z||000017||batboy||03-10-2000||11:25 AM||||Smokey, I've never used nitrous on any of my cars and probably never will. It is very hard on an engine as most people know. We all have our own opinions. Although I don't care for nitrous, personally, I don't think less of someone who uses the "gas" to get an edge. All's fair in love, war, and racing! But, the name calling... shame on you!<P>88Formula, I've been trying to convert the masses too. Torque rules, horsepower drools. Torque will win the stoplight Grand Prix nearly everytime. If you're after more torque, then my other saying is: there's no replacement for displacement. Hope that's clear as mud!||||reg||1
