Z||000019||Greg Piet||03-10-2000||05:48 PM||||I suppose as far as nitrous goes im sitting on the fence.   I wouldnt use it, becuase I was brought up (notice im emphasizing brought up)as it being "cheater fuel", or a replacement for a fast car because you dont have the skill or gumption to make it go fast any other way.  HOWEVER... If someone wants to use it, thats fine, but if I get toasted because someone is running NOS I dont consider it a significant loss since im not running it.  I have never put NOS in the same category as a supercharger, primarily because the NOS bottle runs out, but the supercharger just keeps going and going and going (untill you run out of GASOLINE).<P>There is a reason why certain cars run racing fuel, or nitromethane, but image a NASCAR race with each team running their own magical fuel mixture.  That just doesnt seem right.  Since here we are dealing primarily with street cars I think Unleaded should be the fuel.  <P>I also started autocrossing, and the rulebook there states that we are required to run standard fuel that can be purchased at any local gas station (I guess that measns I cant go buy a drum of 120 octane leaded racing fuel and race with it at the next autocross).<P>So now you folks can pick on me as well as Smokey. ||||reg||1
