Z||000027||Greg Piet||03-12-2000||05:41 AM||||Where did you put your Street Racing Handbook?<BR>Well I dont know about that, but it might have the words DMV on the cover, and somewhere inside the book stating what the top speed is in your state.  <BR>But in all seriousness...  There ARE rules  whether they are spoken prior to the race, or the unspoken variety which always vary from location to location.  If there isnt a line drawn somewhere, then I suppose it would be OK for anyone to put a few short range missiles on the roof of their car, and blow the hell out of anyone that got ahead of them.  So if you want to have a NOS race thats just dandy, but im of the opinion something like that (Or Missiles) should be an agreed upon accessory.||||reg||1
Z||000028||Spyder||03-12-2000||10:14 AM||||OK, I was joking around with the post above.<BR>I wanted everyone to open there eyes and see that there are so many factors involved with a race and a different way to look at it.<P>I used to dislike N20.  I have had a change of heart.  <BR>I would like to have the option of pushing a button to go ahead and spank whoever is messing with me.<BR>As of right now, I do not have N20, but I plan on using it.<BR>I feel like it would work for me since it would only be used when needed.<P>Smokey, <BR>What exactly makes N2O cheating? (seriously, help me understand)<BR>What do you suggest these guys to do to their car to keep up with these rice burners who are using the blue bottle? (an inexpensive way) <P>Again I was just kidding around with the post above, no hate or meanness implied. ||||reg||1
